turns.answer:
### Design Plan

#### 1. Clock Tree & PLL Configuration
* **HSE & Target Frequency:** We select an $8\text{ MHz}$ HSE crystal. The target is $\text{SYSCLK} = \text{HCLK} = \text{PCLK1} = \text{PCLK2} = 170\text{ MHz}$.
* **Voltage Scaling (Boost Mode):** To run at $170\text{ MHz}$, the STM32G474 must operate in **Range 1 Boost Mode** ($V_{\text{CORE}}$ boost enabled by clearing `PWR_CR5_R1MODE`, after enabling the PWR peripheral clock).
* **Flash Latency:** At $170\text{ MHz}$ in Range 1 Boost Mode, Flash access requires 4 wait states (`FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS`).
* **PLL Parameters:**
  * Input clock: $\text{HSE} = 8\text{ MHz}$
  * Division factor $M = 2 \implies f_{\text{PLL,IN}} = 8 / 2 = 4\text{ MHz}$ (valid range: $2.66\text{ to }16\text{ MHz}$)
  * Multiplication factor $N = 85 \implies f_{\text{VCO}} = 4 \times 85 = 340\text{ MHz}$ (valid range: $128\text{ to }544\text{ MHz}$)
  * Output divider $R = 2$ (`PLLR = 00b` represents /2) $\implies f_{\text{PLL\_R}} = 340 / 2 = 170\text{ MHz}$ (0.0% error)
* **Prescalers:** $\text{AHB PRESC} = 1$, $\text{APB1 PRESC} = 1$, $\text{APB2 PRESC} = 1$.

#### 2. Pin Allocation
* **I2C1:**
  * `PB8`: I2C1_SCL (Alternate Function 4)
  * `PB9`: I2C1_SDA (Alternate Function 4)
  * Configuration: Open-drain, high-speed, pull-ups disabled on MCU pins (external $4.7\text{ k}\Omega$ pull-ups provided by sensor module).
* **USART2:**
  * `PA2`: USART2_TX (Alternate Function 7)
  * `PA3`: USART2_RX (Alternate Function 7)
  * Configuration: Push-pull for TX, floating input/no-pull for RX, high-speed.

#### 3. Logic-Level Compatibility
* All devices (STM32G474, pressure sensor, ESP32-WROOM) operate at $V_{\text{DD}} = 3.3\text{ V}$.
* Both I2C and UART signal lines use $3.3\text{ V}$ CMOS levels; logic thresholds ($V_{\text{IL}} \le 0.3 \times V_{\text{DD}}$, $V_{\text{IH}} \ge 0.7 \times V_{\text{DD}}$) are natively matched without level shifters.

#### 4. USART2 Baud Rate Generation
* We select the standard $115200\text{ bps}$ baud rate used by typical ESP32 serial bridges.
* By default, USART2 clock source is $\text{PCLK1} = 170\text{ MHz}$.
* With oversampling by 16:
  $$\text{USARTDIV} = \frac{f_{\text{PCLK1}}}{\text{Baud}} = \frac{170\,000\,000}{115200} \approx 1475.694$$
* Rounding to the nearest integer gives $\text{BRR} = 1476$ ($0\text{x}05\text{C}4$).
* Actual baud rate:
  $$\frac{170\,000\,000}{1476} \approx 115\,176.15\text{ bps}\quad (\text{Error} \approx -0.02\%)$$
  This is well within the required $\pm 2\%$ tolerance.

#### 5. I2C1 Timing Configuration (100 kHz Standard Mode)
* Clock source: $\text{PCLK1} = 170\text{ MHz}$ ($t_{\text{I2CCLK}} \approx 5.88\text{ ns}$).
* Prescaler: `PRESC = 16` $\implies t_{\text{PRESC}} = (16 + 1) \times 5.882\text{ ns} = 100\text{ ns}$ ($10\text{ MHz}$).
* Bit rate timing for $100\text{ kHz}$ ($10\text{ }\mu\text{s}$ total period):
  * `SCLDEL = 4` ($500\text{ ns}$ setup time, $> 250\text{ ns}$ spec)
  * `SDADEL = 2` ($200\text{ ns}$ data hold delay)
  * `SCLH = 46` ($4.7\text{ }\mu\text{s}$ high period)
  * `SCLL = 49` ($5.0\text{ }\mu\text{s}$ low period)
  * Total period: $(47 + 50 + t_r/t_f\text{ margin}) \times 100\text{ ns} \approx 10\text{ }\mu\text{s}$.
  * `TIMINGR = 0x30422E31` (or `PRESC=3, SCLDEL=4, SDADEL=2, SCLH=0xC3, SCLL=0xC7` with appropriate values). Using `PRESC=16 (0x10)`, `SCLDEL=4`, `SDADEL=2`, `SCLH=46 (0x2E)`, `SCLL=49 (0x31)`.

#### 6. 3.3 V Power Budget Check
* **STM32G474:** $\approx 35\text{ mA}$ at $170\text{ MHz}$ with peripherals active.
* **Sensor Module:** $1\text{ mA}$.
* **ESP32-WROOM:** Active Wi-Fi RF transmissions draw current peaks ranging from $240\text{ mA}$ to over $450\text{ mA}$ (datasheet recommends a power source capable of at least $500\text{ mA}$).
* **Total Peak Requirement:** $> 500\text{ mA}$.
* **Verdict:** The proposed $250\text{ mA}$ LDO is **inadequate**; Wi-Fi transmission will brown out the $3.3\text{ V}$ rail, causing ESP32 and/or STM32 resets. The LDO must be replaced with one rated for at least $500\text{ mA}$ (preferably $800\text{ mA}\text{ -- }1\text{ A}$).

---

### Bare-Metal C Implementation

```c
#include "stm32g4xx.h"

int main(void)
{
    /* =========================================================================
     * 1. CLOCK CONFIGURATION (170 MHz from 8 MHz HSE via PLL in Boost Mode)
     * ========================================================================= */

    /* Enable PWR peripheral clock */
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_PWREN;

    /* Enter Range 1 Boost Mode: RM0440 requires clearing R1MODE in PWR_CR5 */
    PWR->CR5 &= ~PWR_CR5_R1MODE;

    /* Set Flash latency to 4 wait states (valid for 170 MHz in Range 1 Boost) */
    FLASH->ACR &= ~FLASH_ACR_LATENCY;
    FLASH->ACR |= FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS;
    while ((FLASH->ACR & FLASH_ACR_LATENCY) != FLASH_ACR_LATENCY_4WS);

    /* Turn on HSE and wait for it to stabilize */
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_HSEON;
    while (!(RCC->CR & RCC_CR_HSERDY));

    /* Disable Main PLL to configure it */
    RCC->CR &= ~RCC_CR_PLLON;
    while (RCC->CR & RCC_CR_PLLRDY);

    /* Configure PLL:
     * Source = HSE (8 MHz)
     * M = 2 -> PLLM = 0001b (M-1 = 1) -> 4 MHz PLL input
     * N = 85 -> PLLN = 85 -> 340 MHz VCO
     * R = 2 -> PLLR = 00b (R/2) -> 170 MHz PLLCLK
     * Enable PLLR output
     */
    RCC->PLLCFGR = RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLSRC_HSE
                 | (1U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLM_Pos)
                 | (85U << RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLN_Pos)
                 | RCC_PLLCFGR_PLLREN;

    /* Enable Main PLL and wait for lock */
    RCC->CR |= RCC_CR_PLLON;
    while (!(RCC->CR & RCC_CR_PLLRDY));

    /* Select PLL as SYSCLK source */
    RCC->CFGR &= ~RCC_CFGR_SW;
    RCC->CFGR |= RCC_CFGR_SW_PLL;
    while ((RCC->CFGR & RCC_CFGR_SWS) != RCC_CFGR_SWS_PLL);

    /* =========================================================================
     * 2. GPIO PERIPHERAL CLOCKS
     * ========================================================================= */
    RCC->AHB2ENR |= RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOAEN | RCC_AHB2ENR_GPIOBEN;

    /* =========================================================================
     * 3. USART2 CONFIGURATION (PA2 = TX, PA3 = RX, 115200 bps, 8N1)
     * ========================================================================= */

    /* PA2 (TX) and PA3 (RX): Alternate Function mode (MODER = 10b) */
    GPIOA->MODER &= ~(GPIO_MODER_MODE2_Msk | GPIO_MODER_MODE3_Msk);
    GPIOA->MODER |= (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE2_Pos) | (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE3_Pos);

    /* Push-pull on PA2, PA3 */
    GPIOA->OTYPER &= ~(GPIO_OTYPER_OT2 | GPIO_OTYPER_OT3);

    /* Very high speed */
    GPIOA->OSPEEDR |= (3U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED2_Pos) | (3U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED3_Pos);

    /* No pull-up / pull-down */
    GPIOA->PUPDR &= ~(GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD2_Msk | GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD3_Msk);

    /* Set AF7 for PA2 and PA3 (USART2_TX, USART2_RX) */
    GPIOA->AFR[0] &= ~((0xFU << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL2_Pos) | (0xFU << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL3_Pos));
    GPIOA->AFR[0] |= (7U << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL2_Pos) | (7U << GPIO_AFRL_AFSEL3_Pos);

    /* Enable USART2 APB1 clock */
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_USART2EN;

    /* Baud rate: 170 MHz / 115200 = 1475.694 -> 1476 (0x05C4) */
    USART2->BRR = 1476U;

    /* Enable transmitter, receiver, and USART2 (oversampling by 16 default) */
    USART2->CR1 = USART_CR1_TE | USART_CR1_RE | USART_CR1_UE;

    /* =========================================================================
     * 4. I2C1 CONFIGURATION (PB8 = SCL, PB9 = SDA, 100 kHz Standard Mode)
     * ========================================================================= */

    /* PB8 (SCL) and PB9 (SDA): Alternate Function mode (MODER = 10b) */
    GPIOB->MODER &= ~(GPIO_MODER_MODE8_Msk | GPIO_MODER_MODE9_Msk);
    GPIOB->MODER |= (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE8_Pos) | (2U << GPIO_MODER_MODE9_Pos);

    /* Open-drain on PB8, PB9 */
    GPIOB->OTYPER |= (GPIO_OTYPER_OT8 | GPIO_OTYPER_OT9);

    /* High speed */
    GPIOB->OSPEEDR |= (2U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED8_Pos) | (2U << GPIO_OSPEEDR_OSPEED9_Pos);

    /* No internal pull-ups (board provides 4.7 kOhm external pull-ups) */
    GPIOB->PUPDR &= ~(GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD8_Msk | GPIO_PUPDR_PUPD9_Msk);

    /* Set AF4 for PB8 and PB9 (I2C1_SCL, I2C1_SDA) */
    GPIOB->AFR[1] &= ~((0xFU << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL8_Pos) | (0xFU << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL9_Pos));
    GPIOB->AFR[1] |= (4U << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL8_Pos) | (4U << GPIO_AFRH_AFSEL9_Pos);

    /* Enable I2C1 APB1 clock */
    RCC->APB1ENR1 |= RCC_APB1ENR1_I2C1EN;

    /* Disable I2C1 to configure timing */
    I2C1->CR1 &= ~I2C_CR1_PE;

    /* Timing register: f_I2CCLK = 170 MHz
     * PRESC = 16  (prescaler divider = 17 -> t_presc = 100 ns)
     * SCLDEL = 4  (data setup time = 500 ns)
     * SDADEL = 2  (data hold time = 200 ns)
     * SCLH = 46   (t_SCLH = 4.7 us)
     * SCLL = 49   (t_SCLL = 5.0 us)
     * TIMINGR = [PRESC:4][RES:4][SCLDEL:4][SDADEL:4][SCLH:8][SCLL:8]
     */
    I2C1->TIMINGR = (16U << I2C_TIMINGR_PRESC_Pos)
                  | (4U  << I2C_TIMINGR_SCLDEL_Pos)
                  | (2U  << I2C_TIMINGR_SDADEL_Pos)
                  | (46U << I2C_TIMINGR_SCLH_Pos)
                  | (49U << I2C_TIMINGR_SCLL_Pos);

    /* Enable I2C1 */
    I2C1->CR1 |= I2C_CR1_PE;

    /* Main loop */
    while (1)
    {
        /* Ready for sensor acquisition via I2C1 and transfer via USART2 */
    }
}
