   - Driving **PC5** directly with the 5 V swing from the LiDAR without external level translation violates the Absolute Maximum Rating and risks permanently damaging the microcontroller.
   - Because the board has no room for extra level-shifting components, the RX function is re-routed to **PB7**, which has a 5 V-tolerant `FT_f` I/O structure (maximum input voltage 5.5 V) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.60, 84] and supports `USART1_RX` on Alternate Function 7 (AF7) [STM32G474_Datasheet p.74].

2. **5 V Input Requirements on FT Pins:**
   - Datasheet Table 17 Note specifies that when an FT pin input exceeds $\min(V_{DD}, V_{DDA}) + 0.3\text{ V}$ (here $3.3\text{ V} + 0.3\text{ V} = 3.6\text{ V}$), internal pull-up and pull-down resistors must be disabled [STM32G474_Datasheet p.84].
   - `GPIOB->PUPDR` bits for pin 7 are explicitly cleared to ensure floating (`00b`) input.

3. **Baud Rate & Clocks:**
   - With PCLK2 = 170 MHz and standard 16x oversampling (`OVER8 = 0`), $\text{BRR} = \text{round}(170\,000\,000 / 230\,400) = 738$ (`0x02E2`), providing 230352.3 baud ($\approx -0.02\%$ error).
   - `USART1->BRR` is written prior to enabling `USART1->CR1`.

