### Enabling the HSE Oscillator on the STM32G474

The High-Speed External (HSE) clock source supports an external 4 to 48 MHz crystal/ceramic resonator or an external user clock signal [STM32G474_RM0440 p.277].

#### 1. Hardware / Bypass Selection
- **Crystal / Ceramic Resonator**: OSC_IN and OSC_OUT pins connect to the crystal with load capacitors. The bypass bit must remain cleared (`HSEBYP = 0`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.276, p.287].
- **External Clock Source (Bypass Mode)**: An external clock signal is supplied to OSC_IN while OSC_OUT is left floating/unconnected. The bypass bit must be set (`HSEBYP = 1` in `RCC_CR`, bit 18) before enabling the oscillator [STM32G474_RM0440 p.276, p.287]. Note that `HSEBYP` can only be written when the HSE oscillator is disabled (`HSEON = 0`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.287].

#### 2. Enabling HSE in Software
1. Set the **`HSEON`** bit (bit 16) in the Clock Control Register (`RCC_CR`, address `0x40021000`) [STM32G474_RM0440 p.287, p.288].
